language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Travelling salesman problem: visit every city exactly once and return to the start, minimising the total rounded Euclidean distance
given locations_dim1, locations_dim2 : int
given locations : matrix indexed by [int(1..locations_dim1), int(1..locations_dim2)] of int
letting n = locations_dim1
$ squared Euclidean distance between every pair of cities, flattened: entry (i-1)*n+j is the pair (i, j)
letting SQ = [ (locations[i,1]-locations[j,1])*(locations[i,1]-locations[j,1]) + (locations[i,2]-locations[j,2])*(locations[i,2]-locations[j,2]) | i : int(1..n), j : int(1..n) ]
$ the Euclidean distance rounded to an integer: the unique d with (2d-1)^2 <= 4s < (2d+1)^2, where s is the squared distance (d = 0 only when the cities coincide)
letting DMAX = 2*max(flatten(locations)) + 2
letting COST = [ sum([ d | d : int(0..DMAX), ((2*d-1)*(2*d-1) <= 4*SQ[(i-1)*n+j]) \/ d = 0, 4*SQ[(i-1)*n+j] < (2*d+1)*(2*d+1) ]) | i : int(1..n), j : int(1..n) ]
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of bool
find u : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..n)
letting MINROW = [ min([ COST[(i-1)*n+j] | j : int(1..n), j != i ]) | i : int(1..n) ]
find cityc : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(0..1000000)
find travel_distance : int(0..1000000)
branching on [x]
minimising travel_distance
such that
$ a city is not its own successor
forAll i : int(1..n) . !x[i,i],
$ every city is left exactly once: one outgoing edge per city
forAll i : int(1..n) . (sum j : int(1..n) . toInt(x[i,j])) = 1,
$ every city is entered exactly once: one incoming edge per city
forAll j : int(1..n) . (sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(x[i,j])) = 1,
$ the route is a single tour: positions u[i] of the cities along the route from the origin, so a successor edge moves one position forward (no subtours)
u[1] = 1,
forAll i : int(2..n) . forAll j : int(2..n) . ((i != j /\ x[i,j]) -> (u[j] = u[i] + 1)),
$ the cost of the edge leaving each city is at least the cheapest edge leaving it
forAll i : int(1..n) . cityc[i] >= MINROW[i],
$ the cost of the edge leaving city i
forAll i : int(1..n) . cityc[i] = (sum j : int(1..n) . toInt(x[i,j]) * COST[(i-1)*n+j]),
$ the travel distance is the sum of the rounded distances of the chosen edges
travel_distance = (sum i : int(1..n) . cityc[i])
